een receiving great reviews from top beauty bloggers of India. We would suggest you check reviews on Amazon and from other beauty bloggers before deciding it yourself. Q: I have dark circles problem. Will this serum help in reducing that? A: Dark Circles are a common problem in men and women of any age. They are caused mainly due to stress, lack of sleep, hormonal changes, dietary imbalance, etc. Since the causes are all-natural, dark circles are therefore easy to treat with natural remedies, a good lifestyle and proper sleep. Blue Nectar Kumkumadi Serum is made up of 26 vital herbs including Sandalwood, Saffron, Lodhra, etc. Sandalwood is known for its ability to fight dark circles naturally. Take 2-3 drops of Kumkumadi Serum and mix it with 2-3 drops of rose water. Gently massage your face and under eyes area, using the tip of your fingers, for 2-3 minutes. After the massage, lie down and keep a cold cucumber slice on each of your eyes for 5 minutes. Doing this regularly for 4-5 weeks will help your skin fight the dark circles in a natural way. Make sure to take proper sleep of 7-8 hours daily, along with the above-mentioned use of Kumkumadi Serum. Herbs-Quotient: Kumkum, Chandan, Lodhra, Patanga, Rakta candana, Kaliyaka, Usira, Manjistha, Tejapatra, Padmaka, Padma, Kustha, Gorocana, Nisa, Laksa, Daruharidra, Gairika, Nagakesara, Palasa Kusuma, Priyangu, Vatankura, Malati, Madhuchista, Sarsapa, Surabhi. How-To-Use: Gently apply few drops on moist face & neck. Use fingertips to gently massage the serum in circular upwards motion. Is-This-For-Me: Kumkumadi Oil for Dark Circles: At night, take two drops of the oil on to your palm and apply on your dark circle with ring finger. Do this for both the eyes and leave it to work overnight. Kumkumadi Oil for Dry Skin: Kumkumadi oil works as a moisturizer in dry skin. Kumkumadi Oil for Acne-Prone Skin: Kumkumadi Oil is suitable for acne-prone skin. When using Kumkumadi Oil as Face Serum for acne-prone skin, wash with mild fa