al Compress Potli Massage Blue Nectar’s Devtvakadi herbal compress potli is a bundle of herbal elixirs and soothing comfort. These little pouches are home to several herbs, each working its magical spell towards your chronic pains, sore muscles, and aching joints. With the goodness of neem and turmeric, a compress with this Ayurvedic treatment for back pain will relieve pain in your joints and muscles. You don't need to check whether your skin type matches this potli; it suits all skin types. What’s In That Potli? Potli Massage Ingredients Here is the great list of all that is tied in the malmal so that the next time you do some potli massage, you are no longer curious about the potli massage ingredients or what's working the magic on your pains. Turmeric: As an ingredient of this Ayurvedic potli, turmeric’s anti-inflammatory properties work with warmth to soothe sore muscles and ease joint pain, reducing inflammation naturally. Neem: Neem purifies the skin during massage, helping reduce skin irritation and bringing antibacterial benefits to any area of discomfort. Flaxseed: Known for retaining heat in this Ayurvedic potli, flaxseed delivers deep warmth to relieve tension in muscles while nourishing the skin with essential fatty acids. Black Sesame: Black sesame enhances blood circulation and softens skin, helping soothe aches and improve skin tone in the massaged area. Jaiphal (Nutmeg): This Ayurvedic potli contains the warmth of Jaiphal, which helps to relax muscles, reduce pain, and provide a grounding aroma that calms the senses. Surjhan Meetha: Pain relief is the primary characteristic of this herbal product, providing comfort to aching muscles and joints and promoting relaxation. Nirgundi Leaves: Nirgundi is an herbal pain reliever, and the product eliminates muscle tension, providing comfort to those with chronic pain during a potli massage. Palash Beej: Palash seeds are used in this Ayurvedic potli to relieve cramps and spasms, promoting relaxation and relie