ely? It is difficult to compare Nalpamaradi directly to Kumkumadi as both derive their effectiveness from different natural ingredients. Kumkumadi comprises saffron and sandalwood amongst other vital herbs while Nalpamradi comprises turmeric. Kumkumadi is specifically developed for facial skin, while Nalpamaradi is crafted for entire body. Q.12 I have problem of skin itchiness during winters. Will this help? Yes, Take a few drops of the oil onto the finger and apply gently on the affected area. Leave it on for 20 minutes, then wash off with luckewarm water. Do this once or twice a day for the result. Q.13 Cd this oil help in skin psoriasis? How to use in that case. Massaged directly onto affected areas of the skin to reduce dryness and irritation as well as to facilitate healing. Q.14 I am looking for evening out of my skin tone. Could Nalpamradi Oil help? Yes, When applied on face on regular basis, blue Nectar Nalpamaradi Tailam helps to lighten complexion and improve lustre. Herbs-Quotient: 16 is the herb quotients of Blue Nectar Nalpamaradi oil. Ayurvedic Herbs like Turmeric, Sesame Oil, Parpata, Ena tailam, Nyagrodha, Udumbra, Asvattha etc helps to repair skin, reduce uneven skin tone and reduce pigmentation. Sesame Oil as a base provides perfect hydration and moisture to the skin. How-To-Use: You can use Nalpamaradi Oil to massage your skin as you would use any other massage oil or cream. Leave it for at least 15-20 minutes after softly massaging the face for few minutes. You can use rose water, or a any mild herbal face wash to remove it. Since this is a turmeric infused oil, it may leave a slight yellowish tinge on the face, which will go away on its own in some time. Use for skin Pigmentation: Gently massage into the skin for few minutes, ensuring the pigmented skin areas are covered. After regular use for 6-8 weeks you can see the improvement. Use for skin brightening:Gently massage on your face in a circular motion untill fully absorbed. Leave it on for 20