{"type":"response","data":{"products":[{"handle":"pain-relief-compress-potli-for-body-back-joint-pain","title":"Devtvakadi Herbal Compress Potli Massage | Ayurvedic Solution for Back & Joint Pain Relief (175 g)","description":"Devtvakadi Potli Massage is an effective Ayurvedic remedy for knee, back and joint pain. Infused with 16 potent Ayurvedic herbs, including Neem and Turmeric, this herbal potli supports muscle relaxation and promotes a comforting effect during massage. When used regularly, it also helps to relieve stiffness, improve flexibility, and support natural body and joint care. Rated 4.88/5 (59 reviews). Use Product: The Ayurveda Lab™- Herbal Compress — Herbal compress therapy in Ayurveda is known as Pinda Sweda. It is one of the numerous time-honoured heat therapies described in the classical texts like the Charaka Samhita. Hot bundles of medicinal herbs were applied to the body after an oil massage as a treatment to help ease stiffness and provide comfort for the joints. Ingredients such as Turmeric and Neem were known for their soothing and detoxifying properties. This ritual, therefore, has been passed down through the ages and remains a cornerstone of care for muscles and joints in Ayurveda. Why Blue: Science-Backed Benefits — Findings: A systematic review found that herbal compresses may help reduce osteoarthritis and muscle pain and could be a viable alternative to standard therapies in managing joint pain and discomfort. Source: National Library of Medicine, 2015. Blue: Ingredients Transparency — All Herbs declared on products in form of Herb Quotient; With more than 150 quality herbs, our products have High Herb Quotient; Free From Harmful Chemicals — All our products are free from harmful chemicals & mineral oils. Blue Nector Title: Why Blue Nectar?. Ingredients Title: Plant Based Ingredients. Benefits Title: Key Benefits. Description Title: Know your Product. Product Footer Description: Blue Nectar | Devtvakadi Herbal Compress Potli Massage Blue Nectar’s Devtvakadi herbal compress potli is a bundle of herbal elixirs and soothing comfort. These little pouches are home to several herbs, each working its magical spell towards your chronic pains, sore muscles, and aching joints. With the goodness of neem and turmeric, a compress with this Ayurvedic treatment for back pain will relieve pain in your joints and muscles. You don't need to check whether your skin type matches this potli; it suits all skin types. What’s In That Potli? Potli Massage Ingredients Here is the great list of all that is tied in the malmal so that the next time you do some potli massage, you are no longer curious about the potli massage ingredients or what's working the magic on your pains. Turmeric: As an ingredient of this Ayurvedic potli, turmeric’s anti-inflammatory properties work with warmth to soothe sore muscles and ease joint pain, reducing inflammation naturally. Neem: Neem purifies the skin during massage, helping reduce skin irritation and bringing antibacterial benefits to any area of discomfort. Flaxseed: Known for retaining heat in this Ayurvedic potli, flaxseed delivers deep warmth to relieve tension in muscles while nourishing the skin with essential fatty acids. Black Sesame: Black sesame enhances blood circulation and softens skin, helping soothe aches and improve skin tone in the massaged area. Jaiphal (Nutmeg): This Ayurvedic potli contains the warmth of Jaiphal, which helps to relax muscles, reduce pain, and provide a grounding aroma that calms the senses. Surjhan Meetha: Pain relief is the primary characteristic of this herbal product, providing comfort to aching muscles and joints and promoting relaxation. Nirgundi Leaves: Nirgundi is an herbal pain reliever, and the product eliminates muscle tension, providing comfort to those with chronic pain during a potli massage. Palash Beej: Palash seeds are used in this Ayurvedic potli to relieve cramps and spasms, promoting relaxation and relieving tension during a massage. Ajmod: It is really good for the muscles and has a warming effect that makes the muscles feel comfortable. It also helps to make the joints more flexible. Sendha Namak: AKA rock salt. It is used in this product. The rock salt helps to clean the skin and get rid of the unwanted stuff. It also helps the skin feel smooth and relaxed with its warmth. Clove is another thing that is used in this product. Cloves have an effect that helps to stop the pain in the muscles right away. The natural warmth of the cloves helps to reduce the pain and swelling in the muscles. Neem Patra is very important in this product. Neem leaves have a lot of good things in them. They help to fight off the bacteria and reduce the swelling. The neem leaves also help to calm down the skin when it's irritated. Rose Flower Dried is used in this product. It is very nice. The rose petals help to make the skin feel soft and relaxed. They also smell very good. Help to calm down the body. Sodium Benzoate is used to keep the product fresh. It helps to keep the herbs in the product from going bad. This way, the product can keep helping the body for a time. Nagarmoth is very helpful. It helps to cool down the body and reduce swelling. It is very nice to use during a massage because it helps the body feel calm and comfortable. Potli Massage Benefits Do these potlis only look magical, or are they really so? Let's discover the potli massage benefits. Increases Blood Circulation Imagine the gentle, rhythmic pressure of a warm potli massage gliding over your skin, slowly awakening and soothing every inch it touches. This potli massage not only relaxes your body but also promotes the gentle and firm flow of blood to the desired regions. Once the blood flow is enhanced, your body receives a boost of fresh oxygen and nutrients, giving your body a beautiful and vibrant glow. With the potli massage, your body is in perfect balance with every stroke, and your muscles are relaxed, giving your body the much-needed flexibility and a sense of inner peace. Ayurvedic Treatment for Back and Joint Pain Potli massage is nature's way of providing you with relief from those aches and pains that linger in your back and joints. The herbal warmth of the compressors in the potli massage penetrates your body, relaxing the tension in your back and joint regions. Every application reaches into sore spots, releasing the stiffness and letting your body unwind. As the warmth opens up circulation, your muscles begin to relax, and a comforting sensation spreads throughout, easing joint discomfort. This holistic comfort is not just about your body; it is about bringing your mind and spirit to a place of profound relaxation and inner peace. Reduces Chronic Pain If chronic pain is an unwanted visitor, Ayurvedic Potli massage has a tried and true solution to provide comfort and relief. Filled with the potent power of nature's allies, flaxseed or Alsi, the calming Ni. Custom Tab Title: Ayurvedic Potli Massage for Pain Relief. How-To-Use: For best results, heat the Potli slightly and apply on affected area with Blue Nectar Devtvakadi Back Pain and Joint Pain Massage Oil. The hot temperature stimulates circulation bringing blood towards the skin surface & opening up the glands. In this process, Ayurvedic Herbs are absorbed in the Skin. Weight: 10.0000. Short Description: Blue Nectar Devtvakadi Potli is a traditional Ayurveda Compress Pouch that may help in cases of Back Pain, Knee Pain and Joint Pain. Presence of 16 Herbs in addition to Neem & Turmeric makes it a strong yet safe and Ayurvedic treatment for body pains. Reviews: Customer Reviews Based on 13 reviews Write a review. Hsn: 300490. Ingredients Content1: Turmeric Turmeric contains an active ingredient called Curcumin that may help in relieving pain. Benefit Content 3: Reduces Chronic Pain Ayurvedic Potli contains vital Ayurvedic herbs like Alsi, Nirgundi, Neem Patra, and Turmeric, which help in reducing chronic pain when used as a hot compress on the body. Benefit Content 2: Relieves Back & Joint Pain Ayurvedic potli massage helps relieve tightness in muscles and joints by improving circulation, relaxing tense muscles and reducing the pain. Benefit Content: Improves Blood Circulation Potli massage improves blood flow to a particular area, soothes discomfort and improves muscle flexibility. Ayurvedic Description: Key Herbs: Neem & Turmeric Use for: Back & Joint Pain Relief Suitable For: All Skin Types. Blue Heading 2: High Herb Quotient. Faq Content3: The potli is gently steamed for 10-15 minutes until it is warm and aromatic. This guarantees that the active herbal components are released effectively, resulting in optimum relaxation and therapeutic benefits. Faq Content6: The product has a shelf life of 3 years from the date of manufacturing. Please refer to the packaging for the exact expiry date. Faq Question5: What is the shelf life of this product?. Faq Content5: Relax after the massage and don't wash the area right away. Allow the herbal oils to seep into the skin for 1-2 hours. Drink warm water and allow your body to naturally detoxify and revitalise. Faq Question5: What do you do after a potli massage?. Faq Content4: Potli should be kept dry after cooling. Do not keep it in an airtight container to avoid moisture. Faq Question4: How do I store Potli?. Faq Question3: How long is a herbal compress steamed?. Faq Content2: Do a mild circular massage for 4-8 minutes on the affected region. Faq Question2: How long should I massage with the potli?. Faq Content1: Potli may be reused 15 to 20 times until it loses its aroma or stiffens. Faq Question1: Is the Potli reusable after heating?. Ingredients Content3: Flaxseed Flaxseed oil helps to reduce soreness in the body and also has other components that improve our overall health as well. Ingredients Content2: Neem Patra Neem leaves contain powerful calcium and mineral content in them, which helps build strong bones. Complete Ingredients Heading: Complete Ingre