{"type":"response","data":{"products":[{"handle":"nalpamaradi-tailam-skin-brightening-oil-face-body","title":"Nalpamaradi Thailam - Skin Brightening Oil with Turmeric for Body and Face (16 herbs)","description":"Nalpamaradi Thailam is a potent Ayurvedic skin brightening oil renowned for its ability to brighten the skin and reduce tan. This skin-brightening oil is made with 16 Ayurvedic herbs, including turmeric and sesame oil, and it helps rejuvenate skin, level out skin tone, and reduce pigmentation. Turmeric is an ancient herb, well-known for its ability to remove tan and improve skin tone. Sesame oil, on the other hand, gives deep hydration and nutrition. Because of its ability to heal and brighten the skin, this powerful herbal mixture is frequently used by brides as part of their skincare routine before their wedding Rated 4.86/5 (162 reviews). Why Blue: Science-Backed Benefits — Findings: In this study, researchers created a new turmeric-based topical gel (microemulgel) and tested it on 34 people suffering from moderate skin rashes and inflammation. The study demonstrated significant improvements in clinical and quality of life parameters for treated lesions compared to untreated lesions (P<0.05), with no adverse effects. Iranian Journal of Pharmaceutical Research (2015). Blue: Ingredients Transparency — All Herbs declared on products in form of Herb Quotient; With more than 150 quality herbs, our products have High Herb Quotient; Free From Harmful Chemicals — All our products are free from harmful chemicals & mineral oils. Use Product: The Ayurveda Lab ™ - Nalpamaradi Thailam — \"Nalpamaradi\" is derived from the Malayalam terms nalpa (meaning four), maram (tree), and adi (base or root) and means \"oil infused with the essence of four sacred trees.\" Nalpamaradi, made using the traditional Sneha Paka method, a lengthy, thoughtful process of simmering herbs into oil, is more than a recipe; it's a meditative alchemy of nature. This age-old recipe, which has its roots in Kerala temple traditions, was originally employed in rituals to cleanse, brighten, and prepare the skin both physically and spiritually. Custom Tab Title: Skin Brightening | Natural Glow. Product Footer Description: Nalpamaradi Thailam - Skin Brightening Oil with Turmeric for Body and Face (16 herbs) You must have heard the famous Indian saying Insaan ke kayi chehre hote hai well this may be true in a philosophical sense but definitely not in literal sense.We all have just one face which has the greatest weightage in determining our look. Since the face or skin is such an important part of our body, don't you think it should be our utmost priority to maintain their health? Beauty standards are always subjective and each one of us are unique in our own ways.Imperatively, we should not be on the backfoot when it comes to being the best version of ourselves. Now, the question arises: what is good skin? Well putting it in simplest words, a good skin is a skin that is tan and blemishes free, looks bright and has adequate moisture. The people may think in order to make skin look good they might have to use so many products but wait, you don't need multiple products.There is a single product for making your skin look beautiful than ever. Yes! You heard it right, a single product - Nalpamaradi Thailam/p> Want to know more? Let's dive in to unfold the magic behind this product. What is Nalpamaradi Thailam? It is a powerful Ayurvedic body oil known for its capacity to lighten skin and lighten tans. This product helps to renew skin, balance out skin tone, and lessen pigmentation. It contains 16 Ayurvedic herbs, such as turmeric and sesame oil. An age-old herb, turmeric is widely known for its ability to lighten skin and get rid of tans. Conversely, sesame oil provides deep nourishment and moisture. Brides commonly use this potent herbal blend as part of their skincare routine prior to their wedding because of its capacity to cure and brighten the skin. Basically, it's an oil that helps in brightening, whitening and de-tanning the skin.Its a healthiest way to retain the young and attractive skin. Key Ingredients Nalpamaradi Oil is a natural skin brightening oil which is known for its properties in removing tan from the skin as well. Its an Ayurvedic product which is made by using following natural ingredients: Nalpamara: also known as the Bark of Four Ficus Trees: 1. Peepal, or Ficus religiosa 2. Banyan, or Ficus benghalensis 3. Microcarpa Ficus (Cluster Fig) 4. Indian figs, or Ficus racemosa, are well-known for their anti-inflammatory, detoxifying, and skin-rejuvenating qualities. Curcuma longa, or turmeric: has antibacterial, anti-inflammatory, and skin-brightening properties. Vitamin C-rich amla (Emblica officinalis) helps to lighten discoloration and increase skin brightness. Haritaki (Terminalia chebula) is well-known for its anti-aging and skin-purifying qualities. Terminalia bellirica, or bibhitaki, aids in the healing and detoxification of the skin. A natural blood purifier that encourages a balanced skin tone is manjistha (Rubia cordifolia). Sandalwood, or Chandana, is a cooling and calming herb that helps to minimize skin imperfections. Sesame oil The formulation's basic oil, sesame oil (Sesamum indicum), is incredibly nutritious and high in antioxidants. Vetiver (Chrysopogon zizanioides) renowned for its ability to chill and hydrate. Nagakesara (Mesua ferrea)Aids in the reduction of dark spots, pimples, and acne What makes Nalpamaradi Thailam unique? Nalpamaradi Oil is a jack of all traits.Its a magical product that consists of 14 different ayurvedic ingredients that performs specific duties under the umbrella of one single goal i.e to make your skin healthier and flawless.It's a single solution for your multiple skin ailments. Nalpamara which is the foremost ingredient of Nalpamaradi Thailam is mainly found in the kerala region of India, carrying the essence and purity of Kerala's soil , the nalpamara plays an important role in rejuvenating our skin.Aside from this, this oil includes 15 other ayurvedic ingredients that we mentioned above, that ultimately helps in overall wellbeing of our skin.The diversity of ingredients and effectiveness makes the Nalpamaradi Thailam or oil stand tallest among other skincare product. Benefits of Nalpamaradi Thailam: Nalpamaradi Oil is a product whose each drop holds a ton of benefits.This product that is a home to 16 different herbs are known the help skin in every aspect.Some of the key benefits are as follows: Whiten & brighten: Ubtan or turmeric which is one of the 16 herbal ingredients that this oil consists of, are the drivers of brighter and whiter skin.The turmeric helps in removing tan, dirt and providing an even tone to your skin which further results in a glowy look. Hydration: Skin without moisture is almost like a plant without water, the skin will dry out and may show cracks, in case it lacks moisture.The Nalpamaradi oil includes sesame oil as one of its ingredient that plays very crucial role in nourishing our skin.The oil along with other herbs enriches our skin with moisture for a healthier look. Acne and Blemishes: Nalpamaradi Oil possess anti-inflammatory and antibac. Blue Nector Title: Why Blue Nectar?. Ingredients Title: Plant Based Ingredients. Benefits Title: Key Benefits. Description Title: Know your Product. Faqs: Q.1 Can i use it on oily skin? Yes, it is suitable for all types of skins. Better to use a herbal body wash after applying Nalpamaradi Oil overnight in case of oily skin. Q.2 How to use it like apply before bath or after? Best is to use before bath. Leave it on skin after application for 30 minutes before you take your bath. It may leave a slight yellowish tinge on skin due to genuine active turmeric extract. Q.3 Can i use this on my 5yrs old kid? Blue Nectar Nalpamaradi is completely natural and does not contain any artificial chemicals. It may be safely used for children. You may also want to check out Blue 